h after inflation from 2.9% to 0.8%. This is a reduction in the growth rate of 2.1%.' P10 also breaks down charges: Entry charge 0.00% (P8), ongoing charge for the fund 0.18% (P8). The report earlier states ongoing platform and investment management charges total 0.44% (from canonical model). The illustration footnote (P10) states: 'There may be charges based on your asset selection which are not taken into account in the final column of this table.'","discrepancies":["The report's RIY figure of 2.1% (Low scenario) is presented as the cumulative ongoing charge impact, but the evidence does not explicitly disaggregate this into component parts (platform 0.21%, fund management, and advice fees) to show how 2.1% is composed.","The illustration (P10) shows a 2.1% RIY impact 'after all charges' but the report does not clearly state whether the initial 3% adviser fee is included in this RIY calculation or applied separately; the illustration uses the term 'All charges' but does not break down whether this includes the initial advice fee of 3% amortized.","The canonical model notes indicate internal inconsistency: fund charge of 0.18% (P8 KIID) plus platform 0.21% would total 0.39%, not the 0.44% stated as total ongoing; the canonical model shows fund charge 0.22% elsewhere, creating arithmetic uncertainty.","The Effect of Switching figure quantifies the monetary impact but does not explicitly state the basis: whether it assumes the 3% initial advice fee is paid upfront from the transfer value or whether it is included in the projection. The report states the client 'need to outperform your current plan by £4,672 in the first year' (P11) but does not reconcile whether this is linked to the Effect of Switching figures or a separate calculation.","The illustration (P10) presents the cumulative impact in nominal terms at mid growth (2.9% before inflation, 2.95% in the canonical model), but the RIY table in the report uses real terms (adjusted for inflation). The guard permits